description:
From Nucleus val-urd (bench 2026-10-02): three refusals the HUB makes carry no SPEC 16.1 detail, so a client cannot tell them apart from each other or from the delegate's own INTERLOCKs:
1. the PAUSE gate (handleIntent step 6): a source-mapped intent the delegate does not admit under PAUSE goes out INTERLOCK with no detail; the delegate is never asked;
2. the resume refusals (ESTOP_ACTIVE / INTERLOCK for override / NOT_HOMED): no detail;
3. CLEAR_REFUSED from a release whose canClearEstop() returned false (rfc-2w2 follow-up): the delegate's reason ("MSW_FLT_N still low", "motion not at rest") reaches only the log.

Proposed fix (design field, unified diff, patch -p1), additive, no wire change, no new delegate method: the existing intentNackDetail(channel_id, code) hook is also asked right after admitsUnderPause() returns false (code INTERLOCK; fallback "paused") and right after canClearEstop() refused a held latch (code CLEAR_REFUSED on the safety channel; "no e-stop latched" when there was none); the resume refusals carry hub literals ("e-stop latched", "override latched: return first", "home required"). The hub.hpp comment on intentNackDetail names the three askers. Nucleus already fills the delegate side (ValenceDevice: admitsUnderPause and canClearEstop set the detail and clear it on entry), so landing this plus a pin bump is the whole of val-urd.

